You are refereeing for the Electronic Journal of Combinatorics. Give a decision-grade opinion, not encouragement.

THE PAPER. 9 pages. The unique minimal equitable refinement of a folded partition of the six-cube.

A finite Zeckendorf-prefix fold partitions the six-dimensional hypercube into 21 cells. That partition is not equitable: two vertices of one visible cell have different neighbour counts into another. The paper determines the exact repair. The unique coarsest equitable refinement is the orbit partition of an affine involution, with 48 cells consisting of 32 singletons and 16 pairs; consequently every equitable hidden realization through which the fold factors has at least 48 states, and equality is unique up to relabeling. The quotient spectrum has multiplicities 1, 5, 11, 14, 11, 5, 1, and the discarded 16-dimensional sector carries the adjacency operator of the 4-cube. The non-lumpability is certified twice over, by an exact residual of one quarter that forbids any intertwining matrix, and by two off-grid eigenvalues of the pushforward kernel.

